{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"KICKOFF — epic 6202 endowed-upset-scaup, 'Bounded disk-ceiling architecture for the Gerrit host'.\n\nTREE (Phase 0 preflight): 6 stories, depth 2, no deeper nesting. All six carry recorded file_impact (scope=paths), so all are executable code leaves. Dependency structure is a SERIAL CHAIN, not a parallel fan-out:\n\n    S0 7dfa livid-blondish-shearwater   Finalize the Gerrit disk-ceiling ADR        READY\n     |\n    S1 aa40 injurious-wellmade-moth     Isolate review-gate scratch on its own EBS  blocked by S0\n     |\n     +-- S2 9183 geode-joking-cockatiel   Cap Docker overlay2 + BuildKit cache      blocked by S1\n     +-- S3 e956 divine-streaky-betafish  Bound journald storage                    blocked by S1\n     +-- S4 2ba3 unmelted-grieving-blowfish Bound /var/tmp growth                   blocked by S1\n     +-- S5 910b francium-written-squid   Bound writable container layers           blocked by S1\n\nS2-S5 unblock TOGETHER but are NOT file-disjoint — all four touch infra/scripts/observability.sh, infra/scripts/compose-up.sh and infra/scripts/install-disk-ceilings.sh. Per the skill, parallel worktrees are only licensed for genuinely disjoint leaves, so this lands as ONE SIX-CHANGE STACK in order S0 -> S1 -> S2 -> S3 -> S4 -> S5, matching the dependency order.\n\nLANDING METHOD (discovered, per AGENTS.md/CONTRIBUTING.md): rebar/Gerrit default. Each change pushed to refs/for/main as a stacked relation chain; every commit carries a rebar-ticket trailer plus a DCO sign-off with the commit-msg hook stamping Change-Id; two independent votes gate each change (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1); a ticket closes only after its change is Verified +1; the stack lands by submitting its top.\n\nWORKTREE: /Users/joeoakhart/reb-6202-disk-ceiling, branch reb-6202-disk-ceiling, branched from origin/main at ebbcd7a030d6. Worktree venv confirmed first on PATH (rebar resolves to the worktree binary).\n\nPHASE 2 IN PROGRESS: the epic claim is gated by plan-review; rebar review-plan 6202 is running. Earning the epic attestation now is deliberate — it prevents the parent-first claim cascade from hitting that same gate on the first leaf claim.\n\nOPERATOR CONTEXT carried in: the design is firm and must not be re-litigated. Option A (per-accumulator hard caps via native GC, each capped generator carrying its OWN CloudWatch alarm) and Option C (separate EBS for review scratch) are both operator-approved. Root stays 60 GiB — headroom, not the fix. Defect 2 (alarm missing-data) stays on bug 3276 and is already landed and applied live."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788477071425261001,"uuid":"82600642-ae26-4ddd-9cb1-51f6350e9773"}